The fopen() function is used to open a file in a specified mode, such as read, write, or append. It returns a file pointer (FILE *) that is used for performing file operations.Opens an existing file or creates a new file, depending on the selected mode.Returns a valid file pointer on success, or NULL if the file cannot be opened.
            C

    #include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

int main(){
    FILE* fptr;

    // Creates a file "demo_file"
    // with file access as write mode
    fptr = fopen("demo_file.txt", "w+");

